<title>NORWAY: Norsk Hydro 1996 pre-tax falls 7 pct.</title>
<headline>Norsk Hydro 1996 pre-tax falls 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating revenues	   84,840    vs	79,732</p>
<p> Operating income		9,653    vs	10,704</p>
<p> Result before tax	    10,277    vs	11,089</p>
<p> Result after tax		6,204    vs	 7,133</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian energy, fertilisers, chemicals and metals group is Norsk Hydro ASA. In January the company said it would make provisions and writedown the carrying value of the assets in the North Sea's Frigg area by a total of 600 million crowns in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 10 analysts forecast an operating result of 10.93 billion crowns and a pre-tax profit of 11.52 billion crowns. Six analysts recommended to buy the share, three said hold and one decline to give a view.  </p>
<p> Depreciation		    6,725    vs	 5,992</p>
<p> Other operating costs	67,462    vs	62,281</p>
<p> Writedowns and losses	 1,000    vs	   755</p>
<p>Income from associated</p>
<p>		   companies	 630    vs	   744</p>
<p> Net financial items    minus  219    vs  minus  442</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
